{"availability":"available","full":"henry-luo/lambda","name":"lambda","description":"A modern, general-purpose, pure functional programming language (Alpha)","category":"Productivity","language":"C++","stars":15,"forks":0,"created":"2025-07-09T04:45:01Z","updated":"2026-10-03T06:54:50Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://henry-luo.github.io/lambda/","topics":["doc-engine","functional-programming","markdown","query-language","reactiveui","schema","template-engine","type-first","validate"],"demo":null,"color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z","stars":15,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A general-purpose, cross-platform, functional scripting language and document processing engine in a single 20 MB executable, built from scratch in C/C++.","Internally, Lambda treats documents as structured data. Different input formats (Markdown, Wiki, HTML/XML, JSON/YAML/TOML/CSV, LaTeX, PDF, …) are parsed into a unified Lambda/Mark node tree, transformed with Lambda scripts, validated with schemas, and then rendered via the Radiant HTML/CSS/SVG/JS layout engine.","A stable subset of the literal data model is separately formalised and released as Mark Notation."],"features":["an expressive functional language for transforming data and documents, and","an end-to-end document pipeline (parse → validate/transform → layout → render/view).","Lambda script (pure functional runtime)","Pure-functional core with immutable data structures (arrays, maps, elements) and first-class functions and types.","Expressive pipe operator (|>, with the filter stage |:) for fluent set-oriented data transformation pipelines with inline mapping and filtering."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/henry-luo/lambda/bl